
~(lld-flag)

%% LLD1
#entrance-to-hades
(room *)
(name *)	Entrance to Hades
(look *)
	You are outside a large gateway, on which is inscribed:(line)
        "Abandon every hope, all ye who enter here."(line)
	The gate is open; through it you can see a desolation, with a pile of
	mangled corpses in one corner.  Thousands of voices, lamenting some
	hideous fate, can be heard.
	(if)~(lld-flag)(then)
		The way through the gate is barred by evil spirits, who jeer at your
		attempts to pass.
	(endif)
%% TODO: room action routine LLD-ROOM
(from * go #east to #land-of-the-living-dead)
%% TODO: conditional on flag LLD-FLAG
(from * go #up to #cave2)
(from * go #in to #land-of-the-living-dead)
%% TODO: conditional on flag LLD-FLAG
(prevent [from * go #east])
	~(lld-flag)
		Some invisible force prevents you from passing through the gate.
(prevent [from * go #in])
	~(lld-flag)
		Some invisible force prevents you from passing through the gate.

%% LLD2
#land-of-the-living-dead
(room *)
(name *)	Land of the Living Dead
(* awards 30 points on first visit)
(look *)
	You have entered the Land of the Living Dead, a large desolate room.
	Although it is apparently uninhabited, you can hear the sounds of
	thousands of lost souls weeping and moaning.  In the east corner are
	stacked the remains of dozens of previous adventurers who were less
	fortunate than yourself.  To the east is an ornate passage,
	apparently recently constructed.
	(if)(on-pole)(then)
		Amid the desolation, you spot what
		appears to be your head, at the end of a long pole.
	(endif)

%% TODO: room action routine LLD2-ROOM
(from * go #east to #tomb-of-the-unknown-implementer)
(from * go #out to #entrance-to-hades)
(from * go #west to #entrance-to-hades)
(notice #pile-of-bodies)

%% TOMB
#tomb-of-the-unknown-implementer
(room *)
(name *)	Tomb of the Unknown Implementer
(inherently dark *)
(look *)
	You are in the Tomb of the Unknown Implementer. A hollow voice says:
	"That's not a bug, it's a feature!"
(from * go #west to #land-of-the-living-dead)

%% TOMB
#tomb
(* is #in #tomb-of-the-unknown-implementer)
(name *)	tomb
(readable *)
(dict *)	grave
(appearance *)
	There is a tomb here, made of the finest marble, and large enough for
	four headless corpses. On one end is the cryptic inscription:(line)
	"Feel Free."
(descr *)
	Here lie the implementers, whose heads were placed on poles by the
	Keeper of the Dungeon for amazing untastefulness.
%% TODO: object action routine HEAD-FUNCTION

